From: Honmani <noreply@honmani.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Give the vertical reader an explicit height

In vertical mode the book content is an orthogonal flow (vertical-rl in
a horizontal page). The paginated reader only set a max-height and the
continuous one a percentage height, so the line length was left to the
browser's fallback for orthogonal flows. Desktop Chromium uses the
viewport height; Android WebView 153 on a OnePlus 12 resolved it to 0,
and pages were blank. Set the computed height explicitly in both.

diff --git a/apps/web/src/lib/components/book-reader/book-reader-paginated/book-reader-paginated.svelte b/apps/web/src/lib/components/book-reader/book-reader-paginated/book-reader-paginated.svelte
index f7bb9d6..a27fd4c 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/lib/components/book-reader/book-reader-paginated/book-reader-paginated.svelte
+++ b/apps/web/src/lib/components/book-reader/book-reader-paginated/book-reader-paginated.svelte
@@ -693,6 +693,7 @@
     : undefined}
   style:max-width={width ? `${width}px` : undefined}
   style:max-height={verticalMode && height ? `${height}px` : undefined}
+  style:height={verticalMode && height ? `${height}px` : undefined}
   style:--font-family-serif={fontFamilyGroupOne}
   style:--font-family-sans-serif={fontFamilyGroupTwo}
   style:--font-weight={fontWeight}
diff --git a/apps/web/src/lib/components/book-reader/book-reader-continuous/book-reader-continuous.svelte b/apps/web/src/lib/components/book-reader/book-reader-continuous/book-reader-continuous.svelte
index 5685e66..473b5b2 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/lib/components/book-reader/book-reader-continuous/book-reader-continuous.svelte
+++ b/apps/web/src/lib/components/book-reader/book-reader-continuous/book-reader-continuous.svelte
@@ -663,6 +663,7 @@
     ? `${secondDimensionMaxValue}px`
     : undefined}
   style:max-height={maxHeight ? `${maxHeight}px` : undefined}
+  style:height={verticalMode && height ? `${height}px` : undefined}
   style:padding-left={verticalMode && firstDimensionMargin
     ? `${firstDimensionMargin}px`
     : undefined}
